<div class="min-h-screen bg-white">
  <!-- Hero -->
  <div class="max-w-4xl mx-auto px-6 py-16 sm:py-24">
    <h1 class="text-4xl sm:text-5xl font-bold text-slate-900 tracking-tight">
      Own your data.
    </h1>
    <p class="mt-4 text-xl text-slate-600">
      Create it here. Share it anywhere. Update it once.
    </p>
    <p class="mt-6 text-slate-500 max-w-2xl leading-relaxed">
      A card is your data, stored in one place you control. When you share it, others get a live link—not a copy. You decide who can use it and how. No accounts on ten platforms. No outdated info scattered everywhere. Just one source of truth that's yours.
    </p>

    <div class="mt-10 flex flex-wrap gap-4">
      <a
        href="/cards"
        class="inline-flex items-center px-6 py-3 border border-slate-900 text-slate-900 font-medium rounded hover:bg-slate-900 hover:text-white transition"
      >
        Browse Cards
      </a>
      <a
        href="/cards/new"
        class="inline-flex items-center px-6 py-3 bg-slate-900 text-white font-medium rounded hover:bg-slate-700 transition"
      >
        Create a Card
      </a>
    </div>
  </div>

  <!-- What is a card -->
  <div class="border-t border-slate-200">
    <div class="max-w-4xl mx-auto px-6 py-16">
      <h2 class="text-2xl font-semibold text-slate-900">What is a card?</h2>
      <p class="mt-4 text-slate-600 leading-relaxed">
        A card is a structured piece of public data with a permanent URL.
        It has a front and back, like a physical card.
        It can be embedded anywhere, and when you update it, the embeds update too.
      </p>

      <div class="mt-10 grid sm:grid-cols-3 gap-8">
        <div>
          <div class="text-slate-400 text-sm font-medium uppercase tracking-wide">
            Versionable
          </div>
          <p class="mt-2 text-slate-600 text-sm">
            Every change creates a new version. Content is hashed for verification.
          </p>
        </div>
        <div>
          <div class="text-slate-400 text-sm font-medium uppercase tracking-wide">
            Ownable
          </div>
          <p class="mt-2 text-slate-600 text-sm">
            You control your data. Set terms for how others can use it.
          </p>
        </div>
        <div>
          <div class="text-slate-400 text-sm font-medium uppercase tracking-wide">
            Embeddable
          </div>
          <p class="mt-2 text-slate-600 text-sm">
            One line of code to embed anywhere. Always shows the latest version.
          </p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>

  <!-- Card types -->
  <div class="border-t border-slate-200 bg-slate-50">
    <div class="max-w-4xl mx-auto px-6 py-16">
      <h2 class="text-2xl font-semibold text-slate-900">Card types</h2>
      <p class="mt-4 text-slate-600">
        Cards are flexible. The content is freeform JSON. Some common patterns:
      </p>

      <div class="mt-8 space-y-6">
        <div class="flex gap-4">
          <div class="w-24 shrink-0 text-slate-400 text-sm font-medium">Profile</div>
          <div class="text-slate-600 text-sm">
            Your identity card. Name, bio, links. Share instead of a business card.
          </div>
        </div>
        <div class="flex gap-4">
          <div class="w-24 shrink-0 text-slate-400 text-sm font-medium">Project</div>
          <div class="text-slate-600 text-sm">
            Describe a project or scope of work. Share with collaborators or vendors.
          </div>
        </div>
        <div class="flex gap-4">
          <div class="w-24 shrink-0 text-slate-400 text-sm font-medium">Jurisdiction</div>
          <div class="text-slate-600 text-sm">
            Public entities: governments, agencies, positions. Authoritative public data.
          </div>
        </div>
        <div class="flex gap-4">
          <div class="w-24 shrink-0 text-slate-400 text-sm font-medium">Custom</div>
          <div class="text-slate-600 text-sm">
            Any structured data you want to make public and keep updated.
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>

  <!-- How it works -->
  <div class="border-t border-slate-200">
    <div class="max-w-4xl mx-auto px-6 py-16">
      <h2 class="text-2xl font-semibold text-slate-900">How it works</h2>

      <div class="mt-8 space-y-8">
        <div class="flex gap-6">
          <div class="w-8 h-8 rounded-full bg-slate-200 text-slate-600 flex items-center justify-center text-sm font-medium shrink-0">
            1
          </div>
          <div>
            <div class="font-medium text-slate-900">Create a card</div>
            <p class="mt-1 text-slate-600 text-sm">
              Choose a type, fill in the content, set your terms.
            </p>
          </div>
        </div>
        <div class="flex gap-6">
          <div class="w-8 h-8 rounded-full bg-slate-200 text-slate-600 flex items-center justify-center text-sm font-medium shrink-0">
            2
          </div>
          <div>
            <div class="font-medium text-slate-900">Get a permanent URL</div>
            <p class="mt-1 text-slate-600 text-sm">
              Your card lives at a unique address. Share it anywhere.
            </p>
          </div>
        </div>
        <div class="flex gap-6">
          <div class="w-8 h-8 rounded-full bg-slate-200 text-slate-600 flex items-center justify-center text-sm font-medium shrink-0">
            3
          </div>
          <div>
            <div class="font-medium text-slate-900">Embed or reference</div>
            <p class="mt-1 text-slate-600 text-sm">
              Others can embed your card or fetch it via API. Updates propagate automatically.
            </p>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>

  <!-- Example cards -->
  <div class="border-t border-slate-200 bg-slate-50">
    <div class="max-w-4xl mx-auto px-6 py-16">
      <h2 class="text-2xl font-semibold text-slate-900">Example cards</h2>
      <p class="mt-4 text-slate-600">
        Cards are content-addressable and ownable. Use them for profiles, projects, NFTs, digital wallets, and more.
      </p>

      <div class="mt-10 grid sm:grid-cols-3 gap-6">
        <%= for {card, index} <- Enum.with_index(@cards) do %>
          <%= if index == 0 do %>
            <!-- Three.js enhanced card -->
            <a
              href={~p"/cards/#{card}"}
              class="block group"
            >
              <div
                id={"card-3d-#{card.id}"}
                class="aspect-[3/4] bg-gradient-to-br from-slate-800 to-slate-900 rounded-lg shadow-lg overflow-hidden cursor-pointer"
                data-card-id={card.id}
                data-card-content={Jason.encode!(card.content)}
              >
                <canvas class="w-full h-full pointer-events-none"></canvas>
              </div>
              <div class="mt-3">
                <div class="text-sm font-medium text-slate-900 group-hover:text-slate-700">
                  <%= card.title || "#{card.namespace}/#{card.slug}" %>
                </div>
                <div class="text-xs text-slate-500"><%= card.card_type %> · v<%= card.version %></div>
              </div>
            </a>
          <% else %>
            <!-- Standard HTML card -->
            <a
              href={~p"/cards/#{card}"}
              class="block group"
            >
              <div class="aspect-[3/4] bg-white border border-slate-200 rounded-lg shadow-sm overflow-hidden hover:shadow-md transition group-hover:border-slate-300">
                <div class="h-full flex flex-col">
                  <!-- Card front -->
                  <div class="flex-1 p-4 flex flex-col justify-center items-center text-center border-b border-slate-100">
                    <%= if card.content["front"]["name"] do %>
                      <div class="text-lg font-semibold text-slate-900">
                        <%= card.content["front"]["name"] %>
                      </div>
                    <% end %>
                    <%= if card.content["front"]["title"] do %>
                      <div class="text-sm text-slate-600 mt-1">
                        <%= card.content["front"]["title"] %>
                      </div>
                    <% end %>
                    <%= if card.content["front"]["tagline"] do %>
                      <div class="text-xs text-slate-500 mt-2">
                        <%= card.content["front"]["tagline"] %>
                      </div>
                    <% end %>
                  </div>
                  <!-- Card meta -->
                  <div class="px-4 py-3 bg-slate-50">
                    <div class="text-xs text-slate-400 font-mono truncate">
                      <%= card.namespace %>/<%= card.slug %>
                    </div>
                  </div>
                </div>
              </div>
              <div class="mt-3">
                <div class="text-sm font-medium text-slate-900 group-hover:text-slate-700">
                  <%= card.title || "#{card.namespace}/#{card.slug}" %>
                </div>
                <div class="text-xs text-slate-500"><%= card.card_type %> · v<%= card.version %></div>
              </div>
            </a>
          <% end %>
        <% end %>
      </div>

      <%= if @cards == [] do %>
        <div class="mt-10 text-center text-slate-500">
          No cards yet.
          <a
            href="/cards/new"
            class="text-slate-700 hover:text-slate-900"
          >
            Create the first one.
          </a>
        </div>
      <% end %>
    </div>
  </div>

  <!-- Embed example -->
  <div class="border-t border-slate-200">
    <div class="max-w-4xl mx-auto px-6 py-16">
      <h2 class="text-2xl font-semibold text-slate-900">Embed anywhere</h2>
      <p class="mt-4 text-slate-600">
        Add a card to any webpage with two lines of HTML:
      </p>

      <div class="mt-6 bg-slate-900 rounded p-4 overflow-x-auto">
        <code class="text-slate-300 text-sm">
          <span class="text-slate-500">&lt;</span><span class="text-emerald-400">script</span>
          <span class="text-slate-400"> src</span><span class="text-slate-500">=</span><span class="text-amber-300">"https://public.cards/embed.js"</span><span class="text-slate-500">&gt;&lt;/</span><span class="text-emerald-400">script</span><span class="text-slate-500">&gt;</span>
          <br/>
          <span class="text-slate-500">&lt;</span><span class="text-emerald-400">public-card</span>
          <span class="text-slate-400"> src</span><span class="text-slate-500">=</span><span class="text-amber-300">"https://public.cards/api/cards/..."</span><span class="text-slate-500">&gt;&lt;/</span><span class="text-emerald-400">public-card</span><span class="text-slate-500">&gt;</span>
        </code>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>

  <!-- Footer -->
  <div class="border-t border-slate-200">
    <div class="max-w-4xl mx-auto px-6 py-8">
      <div class="flex flex-wrap justify-between items-center gap-4 text-sm text-slate-500">
        <div>
          Public Cards is an open protocol.
          <a
            href="https://github.com"
            class="text-slate-700 hover:text-slate-900"
          >
            View source
          </a>
        </div>
        <div>
          Early development
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</div>
